WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.880
Speaker 1: Twitter owner Elon Musk says he
is for free speech.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:13.030
One of the realities about being for free
speech is that you have to be for free speech

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.779
or for speech that sometimes might cause uncomfortable
consequences.

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:22.400
This is the reality for so-called free speech
absolutists.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:30.810
We are now learning that Elon Musk limited
tweets in Turkey during the tight presidential

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:37.320
election in which President Erdogan on Sunday
failed to get to the 50% threshold.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.320
And now as a result, that election will go
to a runoff.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.350
There is a Rolling Stone article.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.350
Vanity Fair.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.350
Sorry.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.010
Twitter's Elon Musk Defends Decision to limit
tweets in Turkey during tight presidential

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.010
election.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.890
Oh, is this free speech?

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:57.480
Critics say the social media platform allowed
the Turkish government to silence criticism.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.469
This is an article from a couple of days ago
by Jack McCormick.

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:08.060
On the eve of the most hotly contested Turkish
election in two decades, Twitter moved to

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:14.380
block posts in the country in what critics
argue is a capitulation to a call for censorship

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.040
from Turkish President Erdogan.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:22.630
In response to legal process and to ensure
Twitter remains available to the people of

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:29.579
Turkey, we have taken action to restrict access
to some content in Turkey today.

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:35.140
Oh, A second tweet said the restricted content
would be visible to the rest of the world.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.220
As we know and as the Vanity Fair article
explains.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:42.380
During his 20 years as President, Erdogan
has methodically tightened his grip on power,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.630
undermining key democratic institutions.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:51.060
Adam Schiff, former guest on this program,
tweeted the day before a critical election

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.330
in Turkey.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:57.130
Twitter appears to be acquiescing to the demands
of the country's autocratic ruler, Erdogan,

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.170
and is censoring speech on the platform.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:04.399
Given Twitter's total lack of transparency,
it is hard to avoid the conclusion that Musk's

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:10.770
promises of free speech have again fallen
away.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.599
Twitter didn't say which accounts it restricted,
but Turkish minute reported the censored accounts

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:21.870
include Kurdish businessman Mohamed Jackboot,
who claimed Erdogan staged a 2016 coup attempt,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.930
and investigative journalist Savary Gwan,
who reports on corruption in the country,

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.849
quote, It's a disgrace to democracy and freedom
of expression that Twitter has caved to Erdogan.

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:38.129
Saturday, Elon Musk, Twitter CEO and self-proclaimed
free speech absolutist, defended the restriction.

00:02:38.129 --> 00:02:39.480
Musk said.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.500
Did your brain fall out of your head?

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.519
Responding to Matthew Iglesias, the choice
is have Twitter throttled in its entirety

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:48.110
or limit access to some tweets?

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.110
Which one do you want?

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:56.340
Now, of course, the true free speech absolutist
would say, we are not going to bow to your

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:59.920
authoritarian threats to block all of Twitter.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.690
We will not censor particular tweets at your
demand.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:08.739
And if you do block Twitter in some total,
we will shout from the rooftops and make it

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:12.989
a global story of authoritarian censorship.

00:03:12.989 --> 00:03:17.270
That's how a free speech absolutist would
handle those threats.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:22.900
But Elon Musk said, all right, we'll limit
the content that Erdogan wants limited.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.409
Sadly.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:29.680
This is too common among those who claim that
they are for free speech.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.620
And we've talked about it before with the
MAGA people.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:33.620
Free speech.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.620
Free speech.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:35.620
Free speech.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:36.620
Oh.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.620
Forced Twitter to publish my COVID disinformation.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.769
Otherwise they're bad and we will try to restrict
them or in some some persecute them in the

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:44.879
court of public opinion or potentially even
legally.

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:49.159
Well, then you're not really for the free
speech of that corporation, are you?

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:53.020
Now, is it Twitter's right.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.629
To restrict access to whatever they want.

00:03:55.629 --> 00:03:56.629
Sure.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:03:58.209
No one's denying that.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:06.030
What we're talking about is the selective
application of so-called free speech absolutism

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.420
from self-proclaimed free speech heroes like
Elon Musk.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:11.959
We'll continue to cover it.

